{
  "$comment": "What Cairn reads from and calls on `codex app-server`, checked by the codex-contract lane's `protocol_surface` case against the real pinned binary's `generate-json-schema --experimental`. Maintained by hand: a Cairn change that starts reading a new Codex field, matching a new enum value, or calling a new method adds it here. What Cairn SENDS is not listed: the case derives it from Cairn's own param builders and a live session, and fails on any key the schema does not define. `knownDead` exempts exactly one (method, key) pair each, and every entry names the issue that removes it. See docs/backends.md, 'Managed Codex CLI'.",
